    {
      "block_id": 9,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "DUAL-PLAYFIELD PRIORITY AND CONTROL\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.79782104492188,
        408.40802001953125,
        324.58880615234375,
        418.90802001953125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1427988259649356,
        0.5291081741151412,
        0.540234004493499,
        0.5427113247779106
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 10,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Either playfield 1 or 2 may have priority; that is, either one may be displayed in front of the other. \nPlayfield 1 normally has priority. The bit known as PF2PRI (bit 6) in register BPLCON2 is used \nto control priority. When PF2PRI = 1, playfield 2 has priority over playfield 1. When PF2PRI = \n0, playfield 1 has priority.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.54782104492188,
        441.65802001953125,
        517.3709106445312,
        490.7490539550781
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1423827349027565,
        0.5721848178805774,
        0.8610936470026054,
        0.635784125577374
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 11,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "You can also control the relative priority of playfields and sprites. Chapter 7, “ System Control \nHardware,” shows you how to control the priority of these objects.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.54782104492188,
        505.94903564453125,
        517.326904296875,
        529.3950805664062
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1423827349027565,
